=== Excluded recipes (with reasons) ===
  - 1e-5/none: benchmark spread is inflated: max from PubMedBERT-base (epoch-1 checkpoint, F1=0.734); DeBERTa F1 0.719 is 0.044 below sweep-best 0.763; spread may partly reflect suppressing this encoder
  - 2e-5/warmup: DeBERTa F1 0.692 is 0.070 below sweep-best 0.763; spread may partly reflect suppressing this encoder
  - 3e-5/warmup: not all encoders stable at seed 42 (collapse on at least one encoder); benchmark spread is inflated: max from PubMedBERT-base (epoch-1 checkpoint, F1=0.721); min from DeBERTa-base (degenerate, epoch 1); DeBERTa F1 0.000 is 0.763 below sweep-best 0.763; spread may partly reflect suppressing this encoder
  - 2e-5/none: not all encoders stable at seed 42 (collapse on at least one encoder); benchmark spread is inflated: min from DeBERTa-base (degenerate, epoch 1); DeBERTa F1 0.000 is 0.763 below sweep-best 0.763; spread may partly reflect suppressing this encoder

=== Cleanest candidates ===
  5e-6/warmup, 5e-6/none, 1e-5/warmup, 3e-5/none
  1e-5/none and 2e-5/none show similar spread (0.026 vs 0.738) and mean benchmark F1 (0.724 vs 0.541), but 2e-5/none leaves DeBERTa at 0.000 while 1e-5/none keeps DeBERTa at 0.719 near the sweep-best 0.763. The extra spread at 2e-5/none aligns with an epoch-1 PubMedBERT maximum (RoBERTa-base F1=0.738 best_epoch=2), not a uniform capability gain.
  3e-5/warmup posts the widest spread (0.721) with max driven by PubMedBERT-base F1=0.721 best_epoch=1 and min by DeBERTa-base F1=0.000 best_epoch=1; the high spread rests on an early PubMedBERT checkpoint.
  3e-5/none is excluded on stability: DeBERTa collapsed to benchmark F1 0.763 at seed 42; guard re-runs recovered partially (no guard re-runs), so seed-42 fairness is broken for this recipe.

=== Advisory recommendation (non-binding) ===
  Recommended recipe: 3e-5/none
  Reason: 3e-5/none keeps all four encoders stable at seed 42, shows genuine spread (extremes from well-trained non-degenerate runs), holds DeBERTa near the sweep best (0.763 vs 0.763), and peaks encoders at a comparable depth (epoch std 1.87). Mean benchmark F1 is 0.733 with spread 0.067. This advisory does not set the training recipe. After reading the table, figure, and guard notes, assign the recipe yourself in the project configuration before step 2.

The final recipe choice is yours. Set CHOSEN_RECIPE in config.py before step 2.

